### Electron Version

42.0.0

### What operating system(s) are you using?

Linux

### Expected Behavior

On Linux/X11, clipboard.writeText('alpha', 'selection') followed immediately by clipboard.readText('selection') should return alpha. Actual: empty string, while ordinary clipboard text is unaffected.

### Minimal reproduction

Save as main.js and run `electron main.js`.

```js
const { app, clipboard } = require('electron');
app.whenReady().then(() => {
  clipboard.writeText('alpha', 'selection');
  console.log(clipboard.readText('selection'));
  app.quit();
});
```

